00:39:56,310 --> 00:39:58,870
but how should I pre-train to get the best representation?

917
00:39:58,870 --> 00:40:01,550
What are the properties I'm looking for?

918
00:40:01,550 --> 00:40:04,350
So one property is that you often want your representation

919
00:40:04,350 --> 00:40:06,910
to be somehow small.

920
00:40:06,910 --> 00:40:10,082
You want it to be something that is compact so that--

921
00:40:10,082 --> 00:40:11,290
there's two reasons for this.

922
00:40:11,290 --> 00:40:13,650
One is that this will just use less memory.

923
00:40:13,650 --> 00:40:17,510
You can store low-dimensional, compact features on your disk

924
00:40:17,510 --> 00:40:20,130
with less memory than the raw data itself.

925
00:40:20,130 --> 00:40:21,650
That's the most obvious one.

926
00:40:21,650 --> 00:40:26,700
And the other one is an Occam's razor generalization theory type

927
00:40:26,700 --> 00:40:28,950
of analysis, where you would say that the more compact

928
00:40:28,950 --> 00:40:31,285
representations will be somehow simpler and generalize

929
00:40:31,285 --> 00:40:32,910
better, or learn more abstractions that

